 SmithModel's difficulties (raw 24 to 85 rescaled to 0..1000); bvt/BvtSmith1998 derives them again from the stats.
  sm98-difficulty : List Integer = [426, 491, 524, 557, 524, 655, 688, 836, 442, 836, 836, 836, 754, 786, 885, 918, 1000,
    918, 0, 131, 131, 262, 393, 655, 180, 475, 393, 557, 622, 475, 557, 688, 704, 918, 606, 409, 672, 491, 557, 754, 639,
    442, 590, 655, 409, 754, 786, 803, 737]
  sm98-n : Integer = 49
  sm98-at : List Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm98-at (xs) (k) = if k < 0 | k >= list-length xs then 0 else list-at xs k
  sm98-find : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm98-find (xs) (item) (k) = if k >= list-length xs then -1 else if list-at xs k == item then k else sm98-find xs item (k + 1)
 The menu row of a catalog item, or -1 for an item no 1998 smith makes.
  sm98-index : Integer -> Integer
  sm98-index (item) = if item <= 0 then -1 else sm98-find sm98-items item 0
  sm98-of : Integer -> Integer
  sm98-of (item) = sm98-at sm98-difficulty (sm98-index item)
 blacksmith.m Q4Y7: a weapon's raw value is metal + speed * average damage / 12, armor's metal + 2 * AC; average damage is
 dice * (faces + 1) / 2 + bonus (OUO dice.c CDiceRoll_Average).
  sm98-raw : Integer -> Integer
  sm98-raw (k) = if sm98-at sm98-speed k > 0
    then sm98-at sm98-metal k + sm98-at sm98-speed k * (sm98-at sm98-dice k * (sm98-at sm98-faces k + 1) / 2 + sm98-at sm98-bonus k) / 12
    else sm98-at sm98-metal k + sm98-at sm98-ac k * 2
 The menu lists an item while its difficulty is at most the checked value + 250 and the pack holds its metal.
  sm98-listed : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  sm98-listed (k) (value) (metal) = k >= 0 & sm98-at sm98-difficulty k <= value + 250 & metal >= sm98-at sm98-metal k
 testAndLearnSkill(user, 7, difficulty, 50).
  sm98-skill : Integer = 7
  sm98-range : Integer = 50
 A failure (success = chance - roll, at most 0) loses metal * (-success) / 1000 + 1 of the item's metal (blacksmith.m
 Q4ER), never more than the item takes.
  sm98-loss : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm98-loss (metal) (success) = min metal (metal * (0 - min 0 success) / 1000 + 1)
 A made item's quality: success 600 and up is exceptional (x1.2 in 1998), below 300 poor (x0.8). Lot quality is 0..1000.
  sm98-exceptional : Integer = 1000
  sm98-regular : Integer = 700
  sm98-poor : Integer = 400
  sm98-quality : Integer -> Integer
  sm98-quality (success) = if success >= 600 then sm98-exceptional else if success < 300 then sm98-poor else sm98-regular
  sm98-band-permille : Integer -> Integer
  sm98-band-permille (quality) = if quality >= sm98-exceptional then 1200 else if quality <= sm98-poor then 800 else 1000
  sm98-band : Integer -> Text
  sm98-band (quality) = if quality >= sm98-exceptional then "an exceptional" else if quality <= sm98-poor then "a poor" else "an ordinary"
